LuauG D182: the D3D12 GPU descriptor heaps are written past their end.

Upstream SDL main (checked 2026-09-24) still has both halves of this.

1. D3D12_INTERNAL_WriteGPUDescriptors tests `currentDescriptorIndex >=
   maxDescriptors` once, before copying a group of `resourceHandleCount`
   descriptors -- so a group that starts a few slots short of the end is
   copied past it (the function carried `// FIXME: need to error on
   overflow`). The sampler heap holds 2048; a pipeline with 13 fragment
   samplers reaches its end after 157 draws and the 158th writes six
   descriptors outside the heap. With the D3D12 debug layer on that is
   EXECUTION ERROR #646 INVALID_DESCRIPTOR_HANDLE and a crash; without it, a
   silent out-of-bounds write.

2. When the test does fire, it replaces the heaps in the middle of a bind:
   tables already set for this draw -- and the compute read-write tables set
   at pipeline bind -- are left pointing into the heap that was just
   replaced, which SetDescriptorHeaps makes undefined.

The fix reserves room for everything a draw or dispatch could write BEFORE
writing any of it (D3D12_INTERNAL_EnsureGPUDescriptorSpace), replaces both
heaps there when it does not fit, and marks every table to be rebound -- the
compute read-write tables included, moved into a function so a replacement
can call it. The per-group test now counts the whole group and remains as the
last line of defence.

diff --git a/src/gpu/d3d12/SDL_gpu_d3d12.c b/src/gpu/d3d12/SDL_gpu_d3d12.c
index 8984388..fe69dd5 100644
